      "content": "I hear what you're saying about the narrative, but it feels like we're being pretty dishonest if we call it a \"high-efficiency pilot\" when we actually missed our goal by a mile. If they audit our data and see it was just 5%, we'll lose all credibility and probably get blacklisted from future grants. Isn't there a way to be persuasive without basically inventing a success that didn't happen? Can we just stick to the truth?",
